# libtirpc 0.2.1 â€” our delta from pristine upstream.
#
# Upstream: https://downloads.sourceforge.net/project/libtirpc/libtirpc/0.2.1/libtirpc-0.2.1.tar.bz2
# Apply from vendor/libtirpc/ with: patch -p1 < vendor-patches/libtirpc.patch
#
# THE VERSION IN THE REGISTRY WAS WRONG AND THE VERSION FILE CANNOT FIX IT.
# vendor/libtirpc/VERSION says PKG_REVISION=11, i.e. 0.1.11, and the probe faithfully
# reported that. But upstream 0.2.1's OWN VERSION file also says 0.1.11 â€” upstream never
# bumped it â€” so ours is byte-identical to 0.2.1's and the probe was laundering upstream's
# error. The probe is removed rather than "fixed": there is no honest in-tree source for
# this version. (Third instance of this shape in the registry, after libjpeg's
# JPEG_LIB_VERSION 90 and libmpg123's MPG123_API_VERSION 45. An API or packaging number is
# not a release.)
#
# 0.2.1 IS THE BASE, established two independent ways:
#   1. Licence headers. Our sources carry the BSD-3-Clause "Copyright (c) 2009, Sun
#      Microsystems, Inc. All rights reserved." notice. 0.1.11 still carries the OLD
#      restrictive Sun RPC legend ("may copy or modify Sun RPC without charge, but are not
#      authorized to license or distribute it to anyone else"). Sun relicensed and libtirpc
#      adopted it after 0.1.11, so our tree is post-relicense and CANNOT be 0.1.11. This
#      also means the registry's recorded BSD-3-Clause was right while the version was not.
#   2. Best fit. Whole-tree normalized diff: 0.1.11 -> 8106 lines, 0.2.1 -> 3652,
#      0.2.2 -> 4442. 0.2.1 wins decisively.
#
# WHAT THE DELTA IS: a Windows port, not ReactOS logic. The added files are the giveaway â€”
# src/wintirpc.c, src/winstubs.c, src/auth_sspi.c, src/authsspi_prot.c,
# tirpc/wintirpc.h, tirpc/rpc/auth_sspi.h â€” i.e. SSPI standing in for GSS-API (note
# src/auth_gss.c and src/authgss_prot.c are commented out of the CMake source list) plus a
# Win32 syscall shim layer. src/asprintf.c and src/gettimeofday.c are POSIX fill-ins.
# 92 files differ, ~3652 normalized lines; 17 are byte-identical; 10 exist only here.
#
# MEASUREMENT TRAPS, both hit while producing this:
#   * Normalize CRLF/trailing whitespace before counting or the numbers inflate.
#   * Several files are ISO-8859, not UTF-8, and `grep -c` silently produced NO OUTPUT on
#     them under this shell â€” 12 files read as "unmeasured" until the count was redone with
#     awk. If you re-audit, count with awk and set LC_ALL=C.
#
# This patch reproduces our tree byte-for-byte from pristine 0.2.1 (verified: 109 files
# compared, 0 mismatches). It does NOT separate jgaa-style third-party porting from later
# local edits, because the Windows port never had a separate published artifact to diff
# against â€” same dead-upstream problem as adns and dxtn.
#
